    {
      "seq": 23,
      "kind": "submit",
      "at": 1791589900826,
      "reason": "apply_merges used float('inf') as the \"no merge\" rank. Once min() is holding an int rank, every unmergeable pair makes min/index/count do a mixed int-float comparison, and CPython takes its slow path for those (long_richcompare returns NotImplemented, then the reflected float_richcompare runs). apply_merges now takes an optional inf sentinel, and BasicTokenizer.encode passes max(merges.values())+1. That int is larger than every merge index, so the results are identical, and all rank comparisons become cheap int-int ones. The default is still float('inf'), so other callers (the regex/GPT-4 chunk paths) behave exactly as before. Evaluated: equivalence identical, encode_ir ratio 0.9710, train_ir unaffected (1.0003)."
    }
  ],
